{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q4119785","formula":"Se₂S₆","hill":"S6Se2","elements":["S","Se"],"composition":{"S":6.0,"Se":2.0},"names":{"en":"Diselenium hexasulfide","ru":"Гексасульфид диселена"},"descriptions":{"en":"Selenium hexasulfide is a chemical compound with the chemical formula Se2S6. Its molecular structure is an 8-membered ring, consisting of two selenium and six sulfur atoms (diselenacyclooctasulfane), analogous to the S8 ring, an allotrope of sulfur (cyclooctasulfur or cyclooctasulfane), and other 8-membered rings of selenium sulfides with formula SenS8−n. There are several isomers depending on the relative placement of the selenium atoms in the ring: 1,2-diselenacyclooctasulfane (with the two Se atoms adjacent), 1,3-diselenacyclooctasulfane, 1,4-diselenacyclooctasulfane, and 1,5-diselenacyclooctasulfane (with the Se atoms opposite).","ru":"Гексасульфид диселена — бинарное неорганическое соединение селена и серы с формулой Se2S6, оранжевые кристаллы."},"fame":10,"pubchemCid":null,"mass":null,"charge":0,"smiles":null,"inchikey":null,"iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q15711994","names":{"en":"group of isomeric entities","ru":"семейство химических соединений","uk":"родина хімічних сполук"}}],"structureInfo":null,"structure":null,"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q4119785","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selenium_hexasulfide","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (ru)","url":"https://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%93%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D1%81%D1%83%D0%BB%D1%8C%D1%84%D0%B8%D0%B4_%D0%B4%D0%B8%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BD%D0%B0","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"similar":[{"id":"Q19833487","formula":"PbHgAs₂S₆","names":{"en":"Daliranite"},"elements":["S","As","Hg","Pb"],"fame":5,"kind":null},{"id":"Q2983041","formula":"As₂S₅","names":{"en":"Arsenic pentasulfide","ru":"Сульфид мышьяка(V)"},"elements":["S","As"],"fam